.TH "YAMLR-SIGN" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBCryptographic Manifest Signing & DNA Receipt Embedding\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr sign\fR command signs Kubernetes manifests with cryptographic non-repudiation signatures embedded directly into the manifest metadata annotations \fB[Pro]\fR.
.PP
---
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr sign [path] [flags]
.RE
.fi
---
.PP
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fByamlr sign\fR guarantees supply-chain provenance. It computes the deterministic Semantic DNA hash of the Kubernetes resource AST, signs the digest using local private keys, and records the signature in \fBmetadata.annotations['yamlr.dev/signature']\fR.
.PP
Downstream CI/CD pipelines, GitOps sync processes, and admission webhooks can verify the signature using \fByamlr verify\fR to ensure zero unauthorized alterations occurred.
.PP
---
.PP
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
.RS
# Sign all manifests in the current directory
yamlr sign .

# Sign a specific deployment manifest
yamlr sign ./k8s/deployment.yaml
.RE
.fi
---
.PP
.SH "OPTIONS & FLAGS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fBpath\fR** *(positional, optional)*:
    Path to manifest file or directory to sign. Defaults to \fB.\fR.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--k8s-version <VERSION>\fR**:
    Target Kubernetes schema version context.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB-f, --output-file <PATH>\fR**:
    Path to write signature report (JSON).
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--exit-zero\fR**:
    Always exit with code \fB0\fR.
.PP
